# The repositories that bind this fleet's hooks through a shim.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS.
#
# A shim-contract change must reach every binder, and the capability requires
# each one "verified rather than assumed to have been reached". Until this file
# existed the fleet was enumerated in three places and declared in none: a list
# of absolute paths typed into project-hook-conformance.test.sh, a scratchpad
# script that lived outside the repository, and prose in README.md. Nothing in
# the repository could re-run the propagation check, and — worse — a repository
# MISSING from those lists was indistinguishable from one that passed.
#
# That is Stage-2 finding 7 one level up. ARTIFACTS declares what the installer
# publishes and SHIMMED-HOOKS declares what projects bind, both because an
# expected set discovered from what you happened to find cannot detect a missing
# member. This is the same answer applied to the repositories themselves.
#
# WHY NAMES AND NOT PATHS.
#
# Bare repository names, because a path is a fact about one machine. The fleet
# is checked out under different roots on different machines and in CI, so
# `tools/check-shims.sh <root>` resolves each name beneath the root it is given
# and reports the ones it cannot find. A name that resolves nowhere is reported;
# it is never silence.
#
# WHAT IS NOT HERE.
#
# agenticapps-workflow-core itself. It is the authority rather than a consumer:
# its .claude/hooks/openspec-change-gate.sh is the one self-hosting binder, out
# of profile for byte-identity by ADR-0028. Pass it as an ordinary positional
# argument when you want it scored; do not add it here, or `--fleet` would
# compare the template against itself.
#
# One repository name per line. Blank lines and # comments ignored.

